tags: party_affairs

= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents? 

Currently, the LPS remains our biggest threat. They maintain strong alliances with local newspaper networks that strangle most of our messages outside of the general public. 

[? if year >= 1935 : The threat of the SCPS is always on our backs as well. As a capitalist reform and populist party, they may easily overtake us. ?]

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @anti_lps: We need to focus our attacks on the Liberals.
- @anti_radical: We have to target the radical parties: the SCPS and the CPC(S).
- @anti_scps: Social Credit is the biggest threat to this campaign.
- @anti_establishment: We must take on the establishment: the CPS and the LPS.
- @anti_cpc_s: We need to go after the CPC(S).
- @easy_discard: Let's drop this and move on.

@anti_radical
on-arrival:{! 
Q.enemies = "SCPS and CPC(S)"; 
Q.managerial_strength += 2; 
Q.moderate_strength += 3; 
Q.moderate_dissent -= 3; 
Q.radical_dissent += 3; 
Q.farmers_cpc_s -= 2;
Q.farmers_scps -= 2;
Q.workers_cpc_s -= 2; 
Q.workers_scps -= 2; ; 
Q.cpc_s_relation -= 5; 
Q.scps_relation -= 5 
!}

Attacking Social Credit and 

@anti_scps
on-arrival: enemies = "SCPS"; radical_strength += 5; radical_dissent -= 5; workers_scps -= 3; workers_scps -= 3;
view-if: year >= 1935

Social Credit is a strong populist movement, more amenable to the economic conditions of farmer-dominated Saskatchewan in some aspects than us. It seems a wise choice to target them. 

@anti_lps
subtitle: The dominant party right now
on-arrival: enemies = "LPS"; scps_urgency += 1; workers_lps -= 2; farmers_lps -= 2; new_middle_lps -= 2;

[? if scps_urgency == 0 or scps_seats < 10 : The SCPS is a tiny party right now, with more bark than bite. Many in our party are questioning our choices. ?][? if scps_urgency > 0 and scps_seats >= 10 : The SCPSs are the most urgent problem for us to deal with. ?]

@anti_cpc_s
on-arrival: enemies = "CPC(S)"; managerial_strength += 5; radical_dissent += 8; managerial_dissent -= 5; cpc_s_relation -= 15; cps_relation += 5; pps_relation += 5; workers_cpc_s -= 4;

The party would earn much from distancing itself from the electorally-poisionous Communists

@anti_establishment
on-arrival: enemies = "establishment parties"; radical_strength += 8; radical_dissent -= 5; cps_relation -= 5; pps_relation -= 5; cpc_s_relation += 5; managerial_dissent += 8; moderate_dissent += 8; workers_pps -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1

Targetting the old-line parties earns us populist goodwill.